OL,3,GNEWSACouncil defends drain cleaning
OL,4,Aafter flash flooding
OL,5,
OL,6,FA city council has defended its
OL,7,Fdrain-cleaning programme after flash
OL,8,Fflooding affected businesses and
OL,9,Fresidents.
OL,11,FHeavy rain hit Peterborough on
OL,12,FThursday, causing flooding in areas
OL,13,Fincluding Lincoln Road, St Paul's Road,
OL,14,FCrown Street and the Woodcote Close.
OL,16,FAmong the businesses forced to close on
OL,17,FLincoln Road were the Marina Grill and
OL,18,FThe Crown. The pub's landlord Peter
OL,19,FTurnbull, whose cellar was flooded,
OL,20,Fraised concerns he had not seen "anyone
OL,21,Fcleaning the drains" along the road or
OL,22,Felsewhere in recent years.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,379,370,200,160,0,100
